<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Competition (220)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>competition             (set up a new competition)
competition delete      (choose one to delete)
competition delete &lt;n&gt;  (delete number n)
</pre>
<p>A competition is a race for experience: from its start to its end, the 
game counts how much experience each player who takes part gains, and 
shows the standings on the competition board. Players who qualify are 
added by themselves, with the message "You have been added to ...", the 
next time the game checks them.
</p><p><b>competition</b> opens a menu. Set what you need, then D to save it, or C 
to cancel:
</p>
<ol><li>the competition's name (default: Questing for true power);</li>
<li>the lowest level that may take part (0: no lower limit);</li>
<li>the highest level (0: no upper limit);</li>
<li>player killers only, peaceful players only, or both;</li>
<li>one race, or all;</li>
<li>when it starts, in hours from now (default: now);</li>
<li>when it ends, in hours from the start (default: 30 days);</li>
<li>quests, separated by /: players who have done any of them are left out;</li>
<li>quests, separated by /, meant to be the ones that let players in; at present this list has no effect (see below).</li></ol>
<p>Immortals and morphed players never take part.
</p><p><b>competition delete</b> lists the running competitions with their end 
dates and asks which to delete; <b>competition delete &lt;n&gt;</b> deletes number 
n at once. The command is logged.
</p><p>Note: the menu's labels for items 8 and 9 don't match what it asks when 
you choose them (it asks for "competitions" and "extra flags"); both 
lists are quest names. List 9 is checked, but a player gets in whether 
or not they have done one of its quests.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
